ntainer></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity. </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">I and II only</div></div>",
